      "pattern": "أَمْسِ + [Past verb] + إِلَى + الـ[Place] + وَ + [Past verb] + الـ[Object]",
      "exampleArabic": "أمس ذهبت إلى المدينة وأكلت التفاح",
      "exampleTransliteration": "amsi dhahabtu ilā l-madīnati wa-akaltu t-tuffāḥa",
      "exampleEnglish": "Yesterday I went to the city and ate the apple.",
      "grammarNote": "A closing capstone for levels 21–30: broken plurals (كُتُب، بُيُوت، جِبَال...), full past tense across five verbs (ذهب، أراد، قرأ، أكل، شرب), and وَ joining two complete past-tense clauses — the same joining structure as level 20's capstone, now entirely in the past. جِدًّا ('very') always follows the word it intensifies: بَيْتٌ كَبِيرٌ جِدًّا ('a very big house'), never before it. 30 of 100 levels down.",
